5.2 The Company shall provide a designated supervisor for each shift who shall be the primary point of contact for the Client’s management. The supervisor shall be responsible for coordinating the Staff, addressing any immediate operational issues, and reporting to the Client’s designated manager at the end of each shift.

5.3 The Company shall provide all necessary training to the Staff on food safety, hygiene, and customer service standards. The Company shall also ensure that all Staff comply with the Client’s reasonable policies and procedures, including any dress code and code of conduct.

5.4 The Client shall provide the Company with reasonable access to the Premises, including the kitchen, storage areas, and any equipment necessary for the Staff to perform the Services. The Client shall also provide the Staff with a secure area to store personal belongings and any necessary permits or licences required for the Staff to work at the Premises.

**6. CLIENT OBLIGATIONS**

6.1 The Client shall:

(a) provide the Company with accurate and up-to-date information regarding the Premises, including any health and safety hazards or requirements;

(b) ensure that the Premises are in a safe and operational condition for the Staff to perform the Services;

(c) provide all necessary equipment, utensils, and consumables required for the Staff to perform the Services, except for any items expressly provided by the Company under this Agreement;

(d) provide the Staff with reasonable notice of any changes to the Client’s operating hours, menu, or service requirements;

